{
  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "bridge",
  "diagnosis": "The loop invariant `1 <= i <= a.Length + 1` is too weak. With this upper bound, after the loop exits with `!(i < a.Length)`, Dafny only knows `i <= a.Length + 1`, so `i` may be `a.Length + 1`. Together with `0 <= max_idx < i`, this allows `max_idx == a.Length`, which makes `a[max_idx]` potentially out of range in the invariant and prevents the postcondition `0 <= max_idx < a.Length` from being established. The upper bound should be `i <= a.Length`."
}

